✅ Understanding Amazon EC2 Types, Series & Purchase Options

Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) offers virtual servers in the cloud with different instance families and pricing options to suit every workload.

🔹 EC2 Instance Families

1️⃣ General Purpose – Balanced compute, memory, storage (e.g., t4g, m6i)
2️⃣ Compute Optimized – High-performance CPUs for compute-heavy tasks (e.g., c7g)
3️⃣ Memory Optimized – Large memory for databases & in-memory caching (e.g., r6g)
4️⃣ Storage Optimized – High IOPS and storage throughput (e.g., i4i, d3)
5️⃣ Accelerated Computing – GPUs/FPGA for ML, AI, graphics (e.g., p4d, g5)


---

🔹 Popular EC2 Series

T Series → Burstable performance (low-cost, scalable)

M Series → General-purpose (balanced resources)

C Series → Compute-intensive workloads

R/X Series → Memory-intensive workloads

P/G Series → GPU & ML workloads

I/D Series → Storage optimized



---

🔹 Purchasing Options

✅ On-Demand → Pay-as-you-go, no commitment
✅ Reserved Instances → Up to 72% cheaper, 1 or 3-year term
✅ Savings Plans → Flexible alternative to RIs, cost savings
✅ Spot Instances → Up to 90% cheaper for fault-tolerant apps
✅ Dedicated Hosts/Instances → For compliance & licensing needs


---

💡 Tip: Always choose instance type based on workload + consider cost optimization with Savings Plans or Spot where possible.
